      "content": "Thanks. Just a heads up though, the legal team was pretty firm. They think the more advanced modeling you've been doing in this version is actually what's creating the legal risk, so they're really leaning towards a clean break. They want to make sure we aren't using these specific high-affinity pathways that look too close to the competitor's filings. \n\nOne thing though—I was looking at the Version 2.0 specs. It's so much more limited; I'm worried we're going to lose all the momentum we've gained on these specific oncology targets. Is there any way we can keep the current architecture running in a silo or just tweak the design parameters so it bypasses the patent issues without having to dump everything and go back to the old version?",
